{"ts":"2026-08-30T03:34:16.002Z","type":"finding","frontier":"formation-release-handoff-consumer-parity-main","claim":"NULL CAUSE PINNED deterministically (real ControlPlaneReadinessService on seed and joiner, join-branch fence from the real buildClusterIncarnationFence producer, acceptor-reply-only router evidence): (iii) fence identity — the consumer validates buildAuthorityEvidence(joinerAuthority).fenceIdentity = allowed:current:matched:present:recovered (join branch; or none when the seed-identity read carries no fence) against the seed-published allowed:not_required:unobserved:absent:not_required, so isRetainableAuthority is false on every real joiner; equalizing the fence flips it true. (iv) member connection evidence — a joiner's router holds no bound connection to the OTHER cohort members, so publishedMemberMatchesCurrent also fails (masked behind iii). Authority boot incarnation and durable/cached row projection hold. Fix direction: a typed CONTRACT_VALIDATION_ROLE {AUTHORITY, CONSUMER}; the consumer validates the authority-published fence and treats an absent connection to another member as non-mismatch (a present one bound to another incarnation still mismatches); seed/AUTHORITY semantics byte-identical; seven fail-closed negative witnesses; analyzer classifies revocations at/after the authority's draining event as teardown_truncated. Witness red 2/8 on HEAD -> 8/8; closure tap 136/136 with the line-522 case now a real distinct joiner.","kind":null,"evidence":"scratchpad/consumer-parity/pin-null.mjs; scratchpad/consumer-parity/red.log; test/control-plane/formation-release-handoff-consumer-parity.test.js (candidate)","rulesOut":null,"verification":null,"regressionClassification":null,"scopePressureClassification":null}
{"ts":"2026-08-30T03:34:36.659Z","type":"guard-override","frontier":"formation-release-handoff-consumer-parity-main","code":"blocked-scope","problem":null,"reason":"One atomic consumer-side surface of the formation-release handoff owner: the contract validation role, the consumer fence/member-evidence predicates, the readiness projection that consumes them, the closure-owner restore call site (AUTHORITY role, unchanged semantics), the GCP analyzer classification and its tests, plus the parity witnesses and shard manifests. Splitting the predicates from the validation role would leave the joiner projection inconsistent with the seed contract it must consume. Falsifier: the consumer witnesses must be red on HEAD (2/8) and green after, and the next GCP streak must show joiner barrier events carrying formationReleaseHandoffState active with releaseAuthorized true.","scopeSignature":null,"scopeReauthorization":false}
{"ts":"2026-08-30T04:33:06.839Z","type":"quest-declared","sealed":{"doneWhen":{"probe":"test-receipt","args":{"file":"solve/evidence/formation-release-handoff-consumer-parity.receipt.json","requiredReceipts":["joiner-projects-active-handoff-from-seed-contract","joiner-fence-identity-is-authority-published","joiner-release-authorized-across-spread-reopen","barrier-resolves-ledger-spread-satisfied-from-authority","seed-capture-retention-revocation-unchanged","analyzer-teardown-revocation-not-stranded","budgets-and-single-owner-unchanged","witness-deterministic"]}},"frontierMetrics":[{"probe":"test-receipt","args":{"file":"solve/evidence/formation-release-handoff-consumer-parity.receipt.json","requiredReceipts":["joiner-projects-active-handoff-from-seed-contract","joiner-fence-identity-is-authority-published","joiner-release-authorized-across-spread-reopen","barrier-resolves-ledger-spread-satisfied-from-authority","seed-capture-retention-revocation-unchanged","analyzer-teardown-revocation-not-stranded","budgets-and-single-owner-unchanged","witness-deterministic"]}}],"authoringContractVersion":1,"statement":"A joiner startup-authority projection consumes the seed-owned durable formation-release handoff contract for its own captured generation: projectFormationReleaseHandoff / validateFormationReleaseHandoffConsumerContract on a real joiner (join-branch admission cluster-incarnation-fence states, router evidence from the acceptor IDENTIFY reply only) yields formationReleaseHandoff.state active with releaseAuthorized true and startupAuthorityReady true while the seed retained generation is active across a priority-spread reopen, so the operation-ledger formation barrier resolves ledger_spread_satisfied from the whole-plane authority answer instead of the raw non-monotone spread predicate; the fence identity compared by the consumer is the authority published fence, never a hash of the reader own admission states, and every other consumer-contract predicate (authority boot incarnation, durable-vs-cached row projection, member connection evidence) is validated against what a real joiner holds. The formation-release GCP analyzer classifies a captured generation revoked by a valid disconnect after the authority entered NODE_DRAINING as teardown-truncated, not stranded. Seed-side capture, retention, revocation rules, the 60-second certification window and the single startup-authority owner are unchanged. Root cause from the 2026-08-30 02-15-53 GCP run (generation e1:4a36 [n1,n2,n4] retained 66.6 s across the reopen while joiners n1/n2 sat waiting_for_startup_authority with formationReleaseHandoffState null and reached READY only after the verdict) and from 20 runs since 2026-08-28 with 0/170 joiner barrier events carrying a handoff state.","title":null,"class":"product","constraints":[{"id":"source-change-subagent-verification","statement":"If this Quest changes source code, spawn a subagent verifier before audit and git handoff, then record a Solver finding with evidence subagent:<id>."},{"id":"single-formation-release-owner","statement":"The seed-owned formation-release handoff closure owner remains the sole minting authority; the joiner projection validates and consumes the seed's durable contract and never mints, extends, or locally re-derives release authority."},{"id":"consumer-parity","statement":"The join barrier and bootstrap readiness consume the same whole-plane authority answer the seed published; a joiner-side null projection of a valid retained generation is a defect, never a safe default. Fence, incarnation, epoch and topology checks stay fail-closed for genuinely mismatched contracts."},{"id":"unchanged-budgets-and-owner-rules","statement":"Seed capture/retention/revocation rules, the 60-second GCP certification window and the 120-second internal barrier, readiness floors, and the single startup-authority owner are unchanged. No sleeps, polling acceleration, or readiness weakening."},{"id":"deterministic-first","statement":"Prove through test/control-plane/formation-release-handoff-closure.test.js extended with a distinct real joiner process (join-branch admission fence states, acceptor-reply-only router evidence) red on HEAD and green after, plus an analyzer witness, before any GCP run."},{"id":"no-second-active-authority","statement":"Do not make the harness, analyzer, or readiness owner derive cluster-ACTIVE or READY from nodes.status, publication counts, or coverage; the analyzer change only reclassifies a teardown-truncated generation."}],"verificationTemplates":[],"landingRequirements":null,"frontierIds":["formation-release-handoff-consumer-parity-main"]}}
